                                        "entry_id": "1a4f0cbe-c3da-36fa-85ca-3f898a0ae003",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of expropriating; the surrender of a claim to private property without material compensation; the act of depriving oneself of private propriety rights."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f1c4187-025b-4f57-a0d2-2911ed4275c6",
                                                "sense_id": "377d0ff0-abf8-3ef4-bcf3-d0808d695532",
                                                "text": "c. 1648, Walter Montagu, Devout Essaies.\nThe soul of man then is capable of a state of much peace and equanimity, in the exterior bands and agitations; but this capacity is rather an effect of the expropriation of our reason, then a vertue resulting from her single capacity."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "82ebf4a8-72e0-4aa4-847e-a7a6e5ba05b8",
                        "source_entry_id": "4af034cb-13fa-335e-96d6-14fd6a0808a1",
                        "source_sense_id": "856a741d-6c23-30ad-8df5-c008a03e38ab",
